hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1478","Ali bin Sahl al-Ramli brought us strange news, from Zayd bin Abi al-Zarqa, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abis, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ibn Umm Maktoum, who said: O Messenger of God, the city is full of vermin and wild beasts. He said: “You hear my greeting to prayer, my greeting to The farmer? I said: Yes. He said: “So live happily.”"
